"only, which already hold one. O(n + m).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/findKuratowskiSubgraph()","role":"symbol","title":"findKuratowskiSubgraph()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"findKuratowskiSubgraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KuratowskiSubgraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:9Planarity18KuratowskiSubgraphV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/findkuratowskisubgraph()"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Planarity on undirected graphs. Self-loops and parallel edges never change an answer: the tests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run on the underlying simple graph, read once through the rows in index space. A directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph’s planarity is that of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"graph.undirectedView"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/planarity","title":"Planarity"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph/isPlanar":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the graph can be drawn in the plane without crossing edges (NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"is_planar"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"boyer_myrvold_planarity_test"},{"type":"text","text":"). A simple graph with more than 3n − 6 edges is not,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is answered after counting distinct pairs, before any search. O(n + m)."}],"role":"symbol","title":"isPlanar","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isPlanar","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isplanar","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isPlanar","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"GraphProtocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph/isOuterplanar":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the graph has a planar embedding with every vertex on one face (Mathematica’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OuterplanarGraphQ"},{"type":"text","text":"): whether the graph plus a new vertex joined to every vertex is planar."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A simple graph with more than 2n − 3 edges is not. O(n + m)."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"isOuterplanar","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isOuterplanar","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isOuterplanar","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isouterplanar"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them. Kept apart from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one, and no type is both. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directedView"},{"type":"text","text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs."}],"role":"symbol","title":"Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}]},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph/planarEmbedding()":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/planarEmbedding()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A planar embedding of the graph, over every edge position (loops and parallel copies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included), or nil when the graph is not planar: the witness of planarity (NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"check_planarity"},{"type":"text","text":", Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"embedding"},{"type":"text","text":" output). O(n + m), faces included."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"planarEmbedding"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:9Planarity15PlanarEmbeddingV","text":"PlanarEmbedding"},{"kind":"text","text"